@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>


    <h1>Welcome to My Portfolio</h1>
    
    <p>I built this website for my Graded Unit 2. I chose this project to challenge myself and learn new things, rather than just doing what I already knew. I plan to keep adding to this site and improving it in the future.</p>

    <h2>What I Learned</h2>
    <p>Before starting this project, almost everything used to build it was brand new to me. Here is a list of things I learned how to do:</p>
    
    <ul>
        <li>Use <strong>Blazor</strong> and <strong>.razor</strong> files to build a web app.</li>
        <li>Connect C# to JavaScript using <code>inject IJSRuntime</code> and <code>implements IAsyncDisposable</code>.</li>
        <li>Run live physics math and draw it to a website for my ball game.</li>
        <li>Use <strong>Blobs</strong> and <strong>iframes</strong> to make a live HTML/CSS compiler.</li>
        <li>Use GitHub Actions to host a compiled app, rather than just basic HTML.</li>
        <li>Use CSS to make the layout automatically adjust to different screen sizes.</li>
    </ul>
